From 5ecc45b2df96a9aa48fb0047bd5a94210e77511e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:33:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 22/24] Runner: the tag over the label again, and the tag on
 the results screen

Gibax liked the tag over the 1P/2P label better than in its place, and
the label's colour on it a lot: the routine is version 6 again (the
label, then the tag 1 px above it, centred, twice its texel width), with
the label's colour (lwz r7,0x18(r1)).

The results screen: a racer with a tag shows it instead of its
character's name. The name's quad (bl 0x80008C3C at 0x80526958, in the
rows' function 0x8052667C) calls a second routine (0x80005000, 51 words):
k = lbz 0x1029(r30); no width in the tags' table: straight on to the
game's name; else the tag from our texture, centred in the name's cell,
in the caller's colour, then the game's texture again.

Measured (2 runners, 8 seats, phase 2 runner 94bd7a4 + this code, the 8
racers CPUs at the set-up, SRNP_TAGS=GIBAX,,K-NUX,AMY_R,,WAVE!,,TAILSMKR):
8 finishes, 199 checksums equal, 4 divergences in camera fields only;
both runners show the same results: the five tags, KNUCKLES, NIGHTS, AMY.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
